# rlkwan.msg - Auntie Kwan, madam of the Bilge (San Francisco)
# Plain ASCII only: the English Fallout 2 fonts have no umlauts or typographic quotes.

# Report and payout
{100}{}{The fog came in, the boats came in, and the people who can't go anywhere else came in. Here's the week.}
{121}{}{. Wet money. Everything here is wet.}
{122}{}{Nothing. The Shi's man came before the boats did.}

# Prices and share
{130}{}{Fishermen pay in fish, tanker men pay in scrap, Shi merchants pay in coin and look away. Cheap fills the cabins. Dear brings the merchants.}
{140}{}{Our people keep }
{141}{}{ percent of what they bring in. Where else would they go? Across the sea? There's no ferry anymore.}
{145}{}{A quarter. (Kwan pours tea and doesn't drink it.) The sea takes the rest anyway.}
{146}{}{A third. The same as the tea stall paid. Nobody got rich there either.}
{147}{}{Almost half? (She laughs softly.) They'll say you're a fool. The fog will say nothing.}

# Morale
{150}{}{They sing old ferry songs when the fog comes in. I taught them. My mother taught me.}
{151}{}{They work, they sleep, they watch the water. That's the Bilge.}
{152}{}{They're quiet. The Hubologists come by at night and offer them a clean mind.}
{153}{}{One of them walked into the water last night. The fishermen found her in the morning.}

# Crisis: the drug
{160}{}{One of ours is on Jet. The tanker brings it. She sold her coat for it, and the fog is cold.}
{165}{}{(Kwan watches you work.) Dr. Fung's assistants would not have done that for one of mine.}
{166}{}{Dr. Fung has a room for these cases. It costs, and they don't always come back.}
{167}{}{(Kwan puts the teapot down very carefully.) Jet instead of wages. The tanker men do that with their deckhands. I'll do it. The tea will taste worse.}
{168}{}{Out, then. The docks take everyone eventually.}

# Look
{200}{}{An old woman in a padded jacket who never lets the teapot go cold.}
{201}{}{Auntie Kwan. She ran the tea stall in the ferry terminal when the ferries still ran. Now she runs the Bilge.}

# Construction and staff (her voice)
{460}{}{What do we build? Something the fog can't get into. Then something the Shi can't see into.}
{463}{}{Something you only get in San Francisco.}
{483}{}{Nobody's looking for new faces.}
{484}{}{Our recruiter sits on the pier where the tanker boats land. People who came across the water and can't go back.}
{485}{}{Our recruiter buys debts from the Hubologists and the tanker. The debtors come with the paper.}
{490}{}{I know everyone who ever waited in this hall. Some of them are still waiting. I'll tell them there's a warm room.}
{491}{}{(Kwan closes her eyes for a moment.) Debts. Like the tanker with its deckhands. I'll write the names in the old ferry ledger. Somebody should.}

# First meeting
{800}{}{(An old woman is pouring tea at a folding table on the pier.) Kwan. I sold tea in this hall for thirty years, when the ferries still ran. Now nothing runs. People still come to wait. Rules: tea is free, nobody goes into the water, and the Hubologists stay outside.}
{801}{}{Show me how the house is doing.}

# The Hubologists (Phase 3, 4.3)
{850}{}{The Hubologists.}
{851}{}{The Hubologists come at night and offer the lost ones a clean mind, for a price. The ones who can't pay end up owing them for life. They take the same people we take.}
{852}{}{(You open the back of their "auditing machine" in front of their own recruits: a car battery, two lamps and a needle that moves when you breathe on it.) Half of them walked out that night. Some of them walked here.}
{853}{}{(Kwan sends tea and warm blankets to the doubters on the pier.) They come to us now instead of the machine. The Hubologists haven't noticed yet.}
{854}{}{(Kwan puts down the teapot.) The ones who can't pay their auditing debts will come to us. On paper. The Hubologists get their money, we get the people, and the people get nothing. Is that what you wanted?}
{855}{}{[Science] Their auditing machine is junk. I'll prove it to their own people.}
{856}{}{[Speech] Let their doubters come to us instead.}
{857}{}{[Barter] Make a deal: the debtors they can't use come to us.}
{860}{}{Take on a debtor's note from the Hubologists. ($100)}
{861}{}{(Kwan writes a name in the ferry ledger.) She believed a machine would clean her mind. Now she works off the bill. The Shi are watching the pier.}

